<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ix Chel</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ixchel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ix Chel is a Maya goddess associated with the moon, childbirth, weaving and medicine. In the Postclassic period pilgrims from across Yucatán, especially women seeking fertility and safe childbirth, travelled to her shrines on the island of Cozumel to consult her oracle. Scholars link her with the goddesses shown in the surviving Maya codices, though the exact identification is debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ix-chel.jpg" alt="Ix Chel" width="130" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ixchel_Dresden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
